Q:
Find the following limit using either forms or continuity: lim as x -> infinity of (1-x)^(-3)

A:
0

As x -> infinity, 1-x -> -infinity.

Thus lim as x -> infinity of (1-x)^(-3) = lim as x -> infinity of 1/(1-x)^3.

This is form 1/-infinity which approaches 0.

Thus lim as x -> infinity of (1-x)^(-3) = 0.

